  "rationale": "No prior results, so I seed the two throughput-capable families. The 50 MSPS constraint forces 1 result/cycle, so only pipelined and pipelined_m qualify; iterative/unrolled_k are excluded. I focus data_width 14-18 and n_iter 12-18 because the 2^-12 error bound is met with modest precision plus rounding, and I keep angle/frac guards small to control area/power. pipelined_m is given a smaller share to probe the Fmax/power benefit of multi-stage registers, which is the key lever for the power objective."
}

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "The feasible Pareto front is well-established with 5 distinct designs covering the trade-off space effectively. The minimum power_index achieved is 1.75 (pipelined_m, data_width=17, n_iter=15, m=3) with accuracy_bits=12.7, which satisfies the constraint max_abs_err <= 2^-12 (0.000244141) as 2^-12.72 < 2^-12. The throughput constraint (>= 50 MSPS) is met by all front designs (51.9 to 132 MSPS). The front spans power_index 1.75..4.37 and accuracy_bits 12.7..14.2, providing a good coverage of the objective space relative to the reference point (40, 12). Since this is the final round and the front already contains a clear winner for the selection rule (min power_index) with robust constraint satisfaction, further exploration would not significantly improve the hypervolume or the final design choice."
,
